    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d444">

                <pb facs="1079" n="1067" xml:id="pg1067"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.48/2–745</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        British Secretary of State for Foreign Affairs</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Eden</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Yalta</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-02-10">February 10, 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Eden</hi>: I have received your letter
                    of February 7 on the question of supplies for liberated areas and have read it
                    with much interest.</p>
                <p>In the shortness of time that remains while we are here together I do not feel
                    that I can give this complex and important problem sufficient study to enable me
                    to give you my full comments on your letter. I shall, however, keep the matter
                    closely in mind and immediately upon my return to Washington will give you a
                    full reply.</p>
                <closer>[File copy not signed]</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
